Subject: [PATCH] Land the universe deepener on the box that holds the terminal

The ~100k row cap on every bar file was ours, in four places, and nothing ever re-deepened one.
download_all_symbols SKIPS any (symbol, timeframe) whose parquet exists and refresh_tail only
appends the new end, so every series was frozen at whatever the producer that first created it
asked for; on top of that TERMINAL_MAXBARS (common.ini [Charts] MaxBars=100000) caps M1 and M5
client-side, on every symbol measured, never once at a venue end.

Measured here: EURUSD M30 served 85,712 bars back to 1997-10-10 against 40,136 held; D1 7,789
against 2,268; M15 100,000 to 2022-09-19 against 60,272. XAUUSD -- the only symbol the scalp
lane trades -- held 20,441 M5 bars against 99,999 served, and 20,147 M15 against 99,999.

The deepener PREPENDS ONLY and publishes through universe_registry.publish_frame, so no bar the
judge has read can change under it and it cannot fight refresh_tail over the live end. It floors
every intraday chart at the DENSE frontier: this venue holds only daily bars before ~2019 and
MetaTrader renders each as one bar on every chart, so EURUSD reports the same ~260 bars a year
at M30, H1, H4 and D1 from 1997 to 2018, and splicing that on would be a decade of daily closes
wearing an M30 label. MT5-DeepenUniverse runs it hourly at :47 as SYSTEM, stands down inside the
gold placement windows, and checkpoints its cursor every five symbols.

